If $f$ is continuous on $[a,b]$, differentiable on $(a,b)$, and $f(a)=f(b)$, then some $c\in(a,b)$ has $f\prime(c)=0$. A maximum or minimum is attained; unless $f$ is constant, one extremum lies inside, where the derivative vanishes.

See also: <Rolle theorem>.

