$GL_2(\mathbb C)$ consists of invertible $2\times2$ complex matrices and $SL_2(\mathbb C)=\ker\det$. It is normal, and the first isomorphism theorem gives $GL_2/SL_2\cong\mathbb C^*$.

See also: <Special linear group>.

